From: WC3 Android recomp
Subject: [PATCH] D3D9: forced 3.1.1 compatibility fallbacks

DXVK 3.1.1's required-feature table asks for VkPhysicalDeviceVulkan12Features
::storageBuffer8BitAccess, VK_KHR_maintenance6 and several other extension
features.  The D3D9 frontend never creates 8-bit storage buffers, and its
descriptor bind / push-constant paths have exact core-Vulkan equivalents.
Turnip on Adreno 7xx reports storageBuffer8BitAccess false, and Android's
system Adreno 0.786 driver reports Vulkan 1.3 without maintenance6; either
condition makes DXVK reject the adapter or crash on a null maintenance6 entry
point before D3D9 can render.

When the settings host latches WC3_DXVK_VERSION=3, the archive now treats a
missing extension-provided required feature as a warning and leaves the
feature disabled instead of rejecting the adapter.  The explicit
`dxvk.ignoreMissingExtensions` config option enables the same relaxation for
diagnostic runs; the forced version always wins.  Core Vulkan 1.3 features,
a graphics queue, the push-constant limit and VK_KHR_swapchain remain hard
requirements: without them there is no working device or presentation
surface.  The known command-entry fallbacks are kept: maintenance5 index
buffer binding, maintenance6 descriptor-set/push-constant calls, depth-clip
state, and load-store-op-none attachment operations.

Android's Adreno 0.786 driver also advertises VK_KHR_maintenance5.  The
D3D9 archive keeps explicit VkShaderModule objects as the default path,
which is the path DXVK 1.10.3 uses successfully on the same device.  This
removes one variable from the FF failure but did not by itself make the
SPIR-V 1.6 pipelines compile; the version fix below is the actual cause.
The low-memory placed mapping and all descriptor paths are unchanged.  Set
`dxvk.useShaderModules = false` to restore the maintenance5 path for
diagnostics.

The fixed-function shaders are now generated with `--target-env vulkan1.1`,
which produces SPIR-V 1.3.  The Adreno 0.786 shader compiler accepts the
SPIR-V 1.3 shaders shipped by DXVK 1.10.3 but rejects the 3.1.1 SPIR-V 1.6
variants at pipeline creation with VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN (-13).  The generated
headers add a `D3D9_FIXED_FUNCTION_*_SPIRV_VERSION` macro, and the
`d3d9_fixed_function.cpp` translation unit asserts that each macro is
0x00010300, so a vendor refresh cannot silently restore the 1.6 headers.

Keep the requirements in the D3D11/D3D12 builds; only the WC3 D3D9 archive is
changed here.  See docs/GRAPHICS_DECISION.md and ADR-036.

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_device_info.cpp
@@ -898,7 +898,13 @@
 
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, bufferDeviceAddress, true),
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, descriptorIndexing, true),
-      ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, storageBuffer8BitAccess, true),
+      // WC3 D3D9 compatibility: D3D9 shaders and the D3D9 frontend never
+      // create 8-bit storage buffers.  Turnip's Adreno 7xx driver advertises
+      // every other required feature but reports this one false, which made
+      // DXVK 3.1.1 reject the adapter before D3D9 could initialise.  Keep the
+      // capability required for the D3D11/D3D12 builds; this archive is the
+      // D3D9-only WC3 build.  See third_party/dxvk/patches and ADR-036.
+      ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, storageBuffer8BitAccess, false),
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, storagePushConstant8, false),
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, shaderUniformTexelBufferArrayDynamicIndexing, false),
       ENABLE_FEATURE(vk12, shaderStorageTexelBufferArrayDynamicIndexing, false),
@@ -1060,7 +1066,13 @@
 
       /* Maintenance features, relied on in various parts of the code */
       ENABLE_EXT_FEATURE(khrMaintenance5, maintenance5, true),
-      ENABLE_EXT_FEATURE(khrMaintenance6, maintenance6, true),
+      /* WC3 D3D9 compatibility: Android's Adreno 0.786 driver reports
+       * Vulkan 1.3 without maintenance6, which otherwise rejects the adapter
+       * before the D3D9 frontend starts.  The guarded
+       * blockTexelViewCompatibleMultipleLayers path already falls back, and
+       * dxvk_cmdlist.h falls back to the core vkCmdBindDescriptorSets and
+       * vkCmdPushConstants entry points when the extension is unavailable. */
+      ENABLE_EXT_FEATURE(khrMaintenance6, maintenance6, false),
       ENABLE_EXT_FEATURE(khrMaintenance7, maintenance7, false),
       ENABLE_EXT_FEATURE(khrMaintenance8, maintenance8, false),
       ENABLE_EXT_FEATURE(khrMaintenance9, maintenance9, false),

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_cmdlist.h b/src/dxvk/dxvk_cmdlist.h
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_cmdlist.h
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_cmdlist.h
@@ -622,7 +622,33 @@
     void cmdBindDescriptorSets(
             DxvkCmdBuffer             cmdBuffer,
       const VkBindDescriptorSetsInfo* info) {
-      m_vkd->vkCmdBindDescriptorSets2KHR(getCmdBuffer(cmdBuffer), info);
+      // WC3 D3D9 compatibility: VK_KHR_maintenance6 is optional on Android
+      // drivers, so the extension entry point may be a null pointer.  The
+      // core entry point needs an explicit bind point, so split a mask that
+      // covers both graphics and compute into two equivalent calls.
+      if (likely(m_vkd->vkCmdBindDescriptorSets2KHR != nullptr)) {
+        m_vkd->vkCmdBindDescriptorSets2KHR(getCmdBuffer(cmdBuffer), info);
+        return;
+      }
+
+      constexpr VkShaderStageFlags GraphicsStages =
+        VK_SHADER_STAGE_ALL_GRAPHICS |
+        VK_SHADER_STAGE_TASK_BIT_EXT |
+        VK_SHADER_STAGE_MESH_BIT_EXT;
+
+      if (info->stageFlags & GraphicsStages) {
+        m_vkd->vkCmdBindDescriptorSets(getCmdBuffer(cmdBuffer),
+          VK_PIPELINE_BIND_POINT_GRAPHICS, info->layout, info->firstSet,
+          info->descriptorSetCount, info->pDescriptorSets,
+          info->dynamicOffsetCount, info->pDynamicOffsets);
+      }
+
+      if (info->stageFlags & VK_SHADER_STAGE_COMPUTE_BIT) {
+        m_vkd->vkCmdBindDescriptorSets(getCmdBuffer(cmdBuffer),
+          VK_PIPELINE_BIND_POINT_COMPUTE, info->layout, info->firstSet,
+          info->descriptorSetCount, info->pDescriptorSets,
+          info->dynamicOffsetCount, info->pDynamicOffsets);
+      }
     }
 
 
@@ -1027,7 +1053,15 @@
     void cmdPushConstants(
             DxvkCmdBuffer           cmdBuffer,
       const VkPushConstantsInfo*    info) {
-      m_vkd->vkCmdPushConstants2KHR(getCmdBuffer(cmdBuffer), info);
+      // WC3 D3D9 compatibility: see cmdBindDescriptorSets.  The core
+      // entry point has the same semantics and does not need a bind point.
+      if (likely(m_vkd->vkCmdPushConstants2KHR != nullptr)) {
+        m_vkd->vkCmdPushConstants2KHR(getCmdBuffer(cmdBuffer), info);
+        return;
+      }
+
+      m_vkd->vkCmdPushConstants(getCmdBuffer(cmdBuffer), info->layout,
+        info->stageFlags, info->offset, info->size, info->pValues);
     }

diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.h b/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.h
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.h
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.h
@@ -66,6 +66,19 @@
     /// Maps host-visible memory below 4 GB when the driver and the
     /// platform window allow it. Falls back to a normal mapping otherwise.
     bool lowMemoryPlaced = true;
+
+    /// WC3 forced 3.1.1: accept adapters that lack extension-provided
+    /// required features. Core Vulkan features and VK_KHR_swapchain remain
+    /// mandatory; each ignored feature is logged and stays disabled.
+    bool ignoreMissingExtensions = false;
+
+    /// WC3 D3D9 3.1.1: create explicit VkShaderModule objects for
+    /// pipeline creation instead of chaining VkShaderModuleCreateInfo
+    /// through VkPipelineShaderStageCreateInfo. Some Android drivers
+    /// advertise VK_KHR_maintenance5 but fail to compile pipelines that
+    /// use the pNext shader-module path. Enabled by default in the WC3
+    /// D3D9 archive; set dxvk.useShaderModules = false to opt out.
+    bool useShaderModules = true;
 
     /// Allows full-screen exclusive mode on Windows
     bool allowFse = false;
diff --git a/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.cpp b/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.cpp
--- a/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.cpp
+++ b/src/dxvk/dxvk_options.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,23 @@
     zeroMappedMemory      = config.getOption<bool>    ("dxvk.zeroMappedMemory",       false);
     lowMemoryPlaced       = config.getOption<bool>    ("dxvk.lowMemoryPlaced",        true);
     zeroShaderScratchMemory = config.getOption<bool>  ("dxvk.zeroShaderScratchMemory", false);
+
+    /* WC3: an explicit 3.1.1 choice is a compatibility override.  The
+     * settings host latches "3" into WC3_DXVK_VERSION, so the archive can
+     * keep accepting the adapter when an optional extension is missing
+     * instead of failing startup.  A config option is also available for
+     * diagnostics; the forced choice always wins. */
+    std::string forcedVersion = env::getEnvVar("WC3_DXVK_VERSION");
+    ignoreMissingExtensions = config.getOption<bool>("dxvk.ignoreMissingExtensions", false)
+      || (!forcedVersion.empty() && forcedVersion[0] == '3');
+
+    /* WC3 D3D9 3.1.1: Adreno 0.786 reports VK_KHR_maintenance5 but the
+     * observed FF pipeline failure is consistent with the pNext shader-
+     * module path.  Use explicit VkShaderModule objects by default; the
+     * low-memory placed mapping and the descriptor paths are unaffected.
+     * Set dxvk.useShaderModules = false to restore the maintenance5 path. */
+    useShaderModules = config.getOption<bool>("dxvk.useShaderModules", true);
+
     allowFse              = config.getOption<bool>    ("dxvk.allowFse",               false);
